   "html_text": "Distributive justice and commutative justice do not exhaust the categories of justice with which Suárez works. In addition, there is what he calls ‘providential or governative justice’. This is not strictly speaking justice, but rather designates a feature of good governing for the common good (Schwartz, 2021). When the ruler apportions benefits and burdens to citizens in a manner that is not disproportionate to their merits and demerits, these acts of governing are just, if only in the negative",
